1
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:43,960
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:46,920
[Episode 15]

3
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,430
I've made the pros and cons of the surgery

4
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:52,310
very clear, haven't I?

5
00:01:54,039 --> 00:01:55,070
So I hope you can

6
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:57,070
make a decision as soon as possible.

7
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,510
How about we just don't do it?

8
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,510
It might not even cure me.

9
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:08,400
And it'll cost a fortune.

10
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,520
Who are you putting on

11
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,560
this show for now?

12
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,660
[Please don't spit out the window.
Please put your trash in the trash can.]

13
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,470
Isn't it

14
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:12,750
our money you are talking about?

15
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:13,400
Exactly.

16
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,870
Stop acting like someone's abusing you.

17
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,470
What if the surgery goes wrong?

18
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:17,680
If I end up paralyzed,

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:19,870
wouldn't I really become

20
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:21,079
an old burden?

21
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:23,840
At my age,

22
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:26,570
I'll just live as long as I can.

23
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,710
If one day, I really

24
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:29,280
can't move,

25
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,870
I'll just die on the street,

26
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:32,030
so you'll have peace.

27
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:32,560
Sir, you...

28
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,630
Dad, what are you talking about?

29
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,960
What do you mean by dying on the street?

30
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,310
What would the doctor

31
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,190
[Please don't spit out the window.
Please put your trash in the trash can.]

32
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,360
think of us?

33
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,960
Alright, I'll stop talking.

34
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:42,360
How about you

35
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,680
take more time to discuss it?

36
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:45,310
When you've made a decision,

37
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:46,630
just tell a nurse

38
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:47,829
or the doctor on duty.

39
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:49,740
The office is right next door.

40
00:02:50,190 --> 00:02:50,630
Come on.

41
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:51,960
Now you're not talking.

42
00:02:52,150 --> 00:02:53,030
Why are you playing the victim

43
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:54,290
in front of the doctor?

44
00:02:56,340 --> 00:03:00,870
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

45
00:02:56,870 --> 00:02:57,400
Dad.

46
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,520
You're going to drive Li Zhi crazy
if you keep this up.

47
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,150
We're family.

48
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:02,840
Can't you just make everything clear?

49
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,800
Just stop pushing me!

50
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:06,560
Come on!
I'm just trying to talk this out with you!

51
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,890
How is that pushing you?

52
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,470
What kind of people are they?

53
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:11,270
Why are you so stubborn, old man?

54
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,970
What does it have to do with me?

55
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,120
Why would I be mad?

56
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,680
Like a psycho.

57
00:03:17,079 --> 00:03:17,960
Dr. Che.

58
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:19,800
What are you doing here?

59
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,130
Getting some fresh air.

60
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,079
Why are you here?

61
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,079
I just got a call

62
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:26,590
from a patient's family.

63
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:27,800
I guess things...

64
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:29,150
aren't looking good.

65
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:30,880
I'm here to see what's going on.

66
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,520
Look at me. I forgot

67
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:34,450
you have business at our hospital.

68
00:03:34,630 --> 00:03:36,430
I thought you came to see Dr. Liu.

69
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:42,470
I'm sorry.

70
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,280
You see, sometimes I speak

71
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:45,490
without thinking.

72
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:46,910
It's fine.

73
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,430
It's not a secret.

74
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,150
I did pursue him before.

75
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,280
It's just that it didn't succeed,

76
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,470
and he ran away.

77
00:03:58,630 --> 00:03:59,360
I actually feel

78
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,870
he's not quite good enough for you.

79
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:01,470
Really?

80
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,150
I think so too.

81
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,150
Right?

82
00:04:05,630 --> 00:04:07,890
I mean, besides his good medical skills,

83
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:09,520
his straightforwardness,

84
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,360
and his seriousness in doing things,

85
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,620
he has no other merits.

86
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,470
That's true.

87
00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:16,430
He is so mean.

88
00:04:16,829 --> 00:04:17,829
And he has a low alcohol tolerance.

89
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:18,800
To be honest,

90
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,430
I'm quite charming.

91
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,390
Absolutely.

92
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:22,160
But he still doesn't think
I'm good enough for him.

93
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,040
He deserves to be single forever.

94
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,160
The ad was just posted a few days ago,

95
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,120
and he is already gone.

96
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,310
Isn't this a scam?

97
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,040
Exactly.

98
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:27,630
We even made a special trip

99
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,160
from so far away.

100
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,000
What a rip-off!

101
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,240
What a lousy hospital.

102
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,500
I'm never coming back.

103
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:39,710
[Xiaoximen Hospital] [Liu Zhengliang]

104
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:46,500
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

105
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:53,690
[Accessible Route]
[Hospital Admission Registration]

106
00:04:53,800 --> 00:05:01,040
[Huahai Road]

107
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:58,290
Why is it getting more and more remote?

108
00:04:58,430 --> 00:05:00,160
A good business
doesn't need a prime location to thrive.

109
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:00,950
You know?

110
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,500
[Jiajiale Department Store]

111
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,490
It's just ahead.

112
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,020
This is the one.

113
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:06,310
My family runs it.

114
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,600
Don't mind the small space.

115
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,120
It's kept quite clean.

116
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,750
At the internet cafe,

117
00:05:11,750 --> 00:05:13,070
I promised you the discounted rate

118
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,000
of 50 a day.

119
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:15,600
At this price point,

120
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,190
even if you searched the whole city
with a lantern,

121
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:19,270
you wouldn't find another place like this.

122
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:20,600
See? This one is no good.

123
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:22,830
Also,

124
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,800
I'll lend you my laptop
so you can send out your resume.

125
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,200
I'm a good friend, right?

126
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:29,600
Come on.

127
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,480
You're back so early today.

128
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:37,800
That's rare.

129
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,260
This is a guest I brought back.

130
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,159
I promised him

131
00:05:44,159 --> 00:05:45,000
50 a day.

132
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:46,880
Give him a good room.

133
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:50,880
How many people?

134
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:52,510
Just me.

135
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:54,630
ID card.

136
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,390
Temporary ID card.

137
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:06,510
It has the same validity as a regular ID.

138
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:07,480
I know.

139
00:06:08,070 --> 00:06:09,240
Just checking if it's real.

140
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,040
Look here.

141
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,390
We have rooms available today.

142
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:16,390
I'll upgrade you

143
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:17,480
to a VIP deluxe room.

144
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,870
What style do you like?

145
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:20,310
Anything is fine.

146
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,480
100 as a deposit. Scan here.

147
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,240
Receipt, ID card,

148
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:30,950
room card.

149
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,460
Go upstairs and turn left.

150
00:07:26,190 --> 00:07:27,870
I saved a complete stranger,

151
00:07:28,430 --> 00:07:29,750
lost all my luggage,

152
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:31,720
and moved into

153
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,700
a place I can't even describe.

154
00:07:35,630 --> 00:07:37,190
This is what they call fate.

155
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:55,409
[Page Directory]

156
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:57,560
[Cervical Spine Health:
Current Issues and Pain Points]

157
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,290
[Product Overview]

158
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,740
The night shift is so hard to get through.

159
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,000
But you used to be

160
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,600
the most energetic one on night shifts.

161
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,360
Speaking of which,

162
00:08:05,730 --> 00:08:11,390
[Yellow Emperor's Inner Canon]

163
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,390
no one is more energetic on night shifts

164
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:09,800
than Liu Zhengliang.

165
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,460
That guy is really energetic.

166
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:13,870
How do you think he's doing?

167
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:16,070
[Yellow Emperor's Inner Canon]

168
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:15,650
Has he started his new job?

169
00:08:19,190 --> 00:08:20,120
You're asking me?

170
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:20,830
How would I know?

171
00:08:20,830 --> 00:08:22,030
He didn't contact me.

172
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:29,600
Speak of the devil.

173
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:31,600
He's calling.

174
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,150
Zhengliang.

175
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:35,840
Are you there?

176
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,549
We were just talking about you,

177
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:37,750
and you called.

178
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:39,650
Don't even mention it.

179
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:40,630
I'm in Bengbu.

180
00:08:40,630 --> 00:08:41,510
Bengbu?

181
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,340
The Bengbu like in "Bengbu Turn?"

182
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:45,840
Why are you there?

183
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,480
It's a long story.

184
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:49,480
Anyway,

185
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,510
I lost all my luggage,

186
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,400
and I reported the loss of my bank cards.

187
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,010
The most important thing is

188
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:07,740
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

189
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,320
I'm staying in a

190
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:03,550
very weird hotel right now,

191
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,790
listening to

192
00:09:04,790 --> 00:09:06,450
disturbing noises next door.

193
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:07,550
Damn it.

194
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:11,270
This is the second time
I've heard you say that.

195
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:15,240
You can't blame Xiaoximen Hospital
this time.

196
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,200
What should I do?

197
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:18,870
Do you think

198
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:21,450
Long Dongdong knew it all along

199
00:09:21,750 --> 00:09:22,600
and is messing with me on purpose?

200
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,600
No way.

201
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:27,080
Mr. Long might be unreliable
with small things,

202
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,670
but he's always reliable with big things.

203
00:09:28,670 --> 00:09:30,200
Reliable?

204
00:09:30,390 --> 00:09:31,480
He asked me to go back.

205
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,810
Isn't that ridiculous?

206
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:35,320
How could I go back?

207
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,600
Even if you wanted to come back now,

208
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,630
you couldn't.

209
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:38,830
Right after you left,

210
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,720
they started discussing staff cuts.

211
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,630
Everyone inside

212
00:09:43,630 --> 00:09:46,480
and outside the hospital is panicking.

213
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,050
What do you mean?

214
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:52,950
Alright,
let's not talk about this for now.

215
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:53,960
You...

216
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,600
Just stay put there.

217
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:57,600
Wait a minute.

218
00:09:58,670 --> 00:09:59,480
Hello?

219
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,600
Why not let everyone listen?

220
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:03,320
It's a private matter.

221
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:05,870
I'll go out and talk.

222
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:09,790
He lost everything?

223
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:10,480
Brother.

224
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,670
Do you think he'll come back?

225
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:13,790
Absolutely not.

226
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:17,590
[Yellow Emperor's Inner Canon]

227
00:10:15,030 --> 00:10:17,270
His heart is completely broken.

228
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,000
Do you think Xiaoximen Hospital

229
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:30,760
[Yellow Emperor's Inner Canon]

230
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,600
will really make staff cuts?

231
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:28,510
We're the backbone of this hospital.

232
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:29,000
No matter what,

233
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,440
they won't lay us off.

234
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:36,150
I'm really doomed this time.

235
00:10:36,150 --> 00:10:37,870
Nonsense.

236
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,840
They scheduled you for surgery, right?

237
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,000
How did you know?

238
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:47,580
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

239
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,280
How did I know?

240
00:10:42,630 --> 00:10:43,760
You're so carefree.

241
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,440
Only surgery

242
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:46,640
can make you anxious.

243
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:49,840
No one knows a father better than his son.

244
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:50,630
Get lost.

245
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:53,120
Chief Physician Tong
will be the lead surgeon,

246
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,670
and I'll be the second assistant.

247
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:55,550
Help me think of a way

248
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:56,550
to refuse it.

249
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,630
Refuse it?

250
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:01,520
What surgery?

251
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,670
CAS.

252
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:06,360
It's a minor surgery.

253
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,360
If it were as easy as you say,

254
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,490
that would be great.

255
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:13,320
I told you before.

256
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,630
No surgery is too small.

257
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,960
You even get anxious
about an appendectomy.

258
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,120
Just tell him directly

259
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,270
that you don't want to do it.

260
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:23,080
Come on.

261
00:11:24,030 --> 00:11:25,270
If only it were as simple

262
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:26,240
as you say.

263
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,000
It's just one sentence.

264
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,330
What's so hard about it?

265
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,390
People are just different.

266
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,750
It's not as simple as you said.

267
00:11:32,750 --> 00:11:34,630
Just keep turning in Bengbu.

268
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:40,870
[Dream Garden]

269
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,150
Fine. I'm done talking to you.

270
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:39,150
There's no way to make you understand.

271
00:11:39,150 --> 00:11:40,000
That's it.

272
00:11:50,190 --> 00:11:51,080
[Chen Junnan] [Transfer]

273
00:11:51,110 --> 00:11:51,640
[Tell me if you need money]

274
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:03,320
Come on. How did I steal your money?

275
00:12:03,750 --> 00:12:04,840
Your money was just sitting there.

276
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:05,910
I spent it to save you face.

277
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:06,630
You know?

278
00:12:06,670 --> 00:12:07,720
You should thank me.

279
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,790
I should thank you?

280
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:10,600
Thank you for doing nothing useful
every day.

281
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,060
You don't do any real work.

282
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,320
Come on. What do you know?

283
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:15,360
This is called surviving in society.

284
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,360
If you keep this up,

285
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,360
I really won't care about you anymore.

286
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,790
What are we to each other
that you should care?

287
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:19,510
Don't worry.

288
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:21,840
Even if I die out there,
I won't need you to care!

289
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:22,910
Where are you going?

290
00:12:22,910 --> 00:12:24,170
None of your business!

291
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,600
What are you doing?

292
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,720
I can't tell you off a little,

293
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,390
right?

294
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,670
Just stop nagging.

295
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:46,720
[Dream Garden]

296
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:46,130
Why aren't you in the hotel?

297
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,130
The soundproofing in this hotel
is terrible.

298
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:54,440
Here.

299
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,440
I'm not drinking.

300
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:07,950
[Shop for Sale]

301
00:13:10,630 --> 00:13:12,090
That woman is uneducated.

302
00:13:12,510 --> 00:13:15,440
When she gets angry,
her language gets pretty harsh.

303
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:18,790
However,

304
00:13:18,910 --> 00:13:20,720
she has a saying she always uses:

305
00:13:22,790 --> 00:13:24,720
"No matter how unlucky you are now,

306
00:13:25,790 --> 00:13:26,600
something good

307
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:28,600
might happen the very next second."

308
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:31,240
Do you think that makes sense?

309
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,270
I hope so.

310
00:13:38,910 --> 00:13:39,790
Who is she?

311
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,260
Theoretically, she's my mom.

312
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:45,630
But I've cut ties with her.

313
00:13:49,510 --> 00:13:50,270
Why?

314
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,840
Youth. Rebellion.

315
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:57,510
Living wild and free.

316
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:59,370
You know what I mean?

317
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:06,030
Here,

318
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,480
have a sip to calm your nerves.

319
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,910
I told you I'm not drinking.

320
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:09,720
Just try it.

321
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:25,770
How's it taste?

322
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:26,960
Too sweet.

323
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,630
That'll be 3 yuan.

324
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,790
QR code or cash?

325
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:01,270
Even one sip is 3 yuan!

326
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:06,930
[Flower of Wealth KTV]

327
00:15:08,630 --> 00:15:09,390
What?

328
00:15:10,030 --> 00:15:11,630
You wanna pick up where you left off?

329
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:12,270
Yes.

330
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:14,840
Well, you worked 10 days,

331
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,030
then took off without a word.

332
00:15:16,030 --> 00:15:17,440
You didn't even come to say goodbye.

333
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:18,150
What?

334
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:18,840
Weren't you happy

335
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:20,000
working here?

336
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:20,840
No.

337
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:23,510
I just figured you were busy

338
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:24,750
and didn't want to bother you.

339
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:26,280
I was perfectly happy here.

340
00:15:29,630 --> 00:15:30,150
Jie.

341
00:15:30,150 --> 00:15:31,240
Jie is short-staffed on the first floor.

342
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,390
Go with him.

343
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:33,320
Mr. Wu.

344
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:35,840
I'm here this time to apply for

345
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,390
that job you told me about.

346
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:39,720
The one that pays over 10,000 yuan
a month.

347
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,790
Wh-What?

348
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,240
Mr. Wu, look.

349
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:50,240
Don't the four of us look like a boy band

350
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,510
standing here together?

351
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:52,570
Like quadruplets.

352
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:54,970
You want to be my assistant?

353
00:15:55,150 --> 00:15:56,080
Didn't you say I had

354
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,790
what it takes when I was working here?

355
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,480
Take another look at me. Check out...

356
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:00,440
this physique.

357
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,480
Last time...

358
00:16:03,790 --> 00:16:05,120
Last time, when President Long

359
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:06,000
brought you here,

360
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,360
you might have had good qualifications.

361
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,480
But now that you're here on your own,

362
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:10,480
that's a different story.

363
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:10,960
No matter what,

364
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,890
you have to go through
the hiring process, don't you?

365
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,670
Sure. What's the process?

366
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,840
An interview.

367
00:16:18,630 --> 00:16:19,360
Stand up.

368
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,440
Young man,
what's your educational background?

369
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,200
Fucheng Polytechnic Vocational College.

370
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,460
I studied accounting.

371
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:31,890
What did you do before?

372
00:16:34,270 --> 00:16:36,200
I used to work in a funeral supply shop,

373
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,320
selling urns.

374
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:44,150
I... I don't need to be an assistant.

375
00:16:44,150 --> 00:16:44,790
Is that not okay?

376
00:16:44,790 --> 00:16:46,240
I'll just keep being a waiter, Jie.

377
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:47,600
Zhengguang, just listen to me.

378
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,720
Just go.

379
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:56,380
[Flower of Wealth]

380
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:50,910
Mr. Wu is very superstitious.

381
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,320
If he had known
you worked in the funeral business,

382
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:54,120
you wouldn't have even lasted

383
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,150
10 days as a waiter.

384
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:56,840
Even President Long
wouldn't be able to help.

385
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:58,080
What's wrong
with working in the funeral business?

386
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,200
Everyone has to face their final day
someday.

387
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,390
Yes, that's right.

388
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,120
Everyone knows it in their hearts,

389
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,030
but no one talks about it, right?

390
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:06,750
Anyway, say no more.

391
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,960
The boss is watching from upstairs.

392
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,680
Go away. Go away.

393
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,510
Otherwise, he'll call me

394
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:13,970
and tell me to kick you out.

395
00:17:14,349 --> 00:17:15,310
Just go.

396
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:16,589
Alright, Jie.

397
00:17:20,069 --> 00:17:21,069
How are you doing?

398
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,890
[Gong's Blind Massage]

399
00:17:29,890 --> 00:17:34,010
[Loosen Up Your Muscles and Joints.
Works Like a Charm!]

400
00:17:34,030 --> 00:17:39,010
[Authorized Personnel Only]

401
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:45,440
You hooligan!

402
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,310
You're pretending to be blind, aren't you?

403
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:48,570
I didn't see anything!

404
00:17:50,030 --> 00:17:50,960
How dare you

405
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,310
harass me!

406
00:17:55,110 --> 00:17:56,440
Pretending to be blind?

407
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,240
I'll teach you a lesson for that!

408
00:17:58,350 --> 00:17:59,680
How dare you harass me!

409
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:02,960
As long as there's one

410
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,310
blind masseur with over 5 years

411
00:18:04,310 --> 00:18:05,400
of experience,

412
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:07,600
it can be called a blind massage parlor.

413
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:08,960
How can this be a scam?

414
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,550
It's a national regulation.

415
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:11,880
It's not a scam.

416
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:13,880
I have never said

417
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:14,920
I was blind.

418
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,120
How can this be a scam?

419
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:17,830
Then why were you wearing sunglasses?

420
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:18,720
Can't I just want to look good?

421
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,030
Can't I just want to look cool?

422
00:18:20,030 --> 00:18:21,160
Who says someone wearing sunglasses

423
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,310
has to be blind?

424
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:23,070
Then when that lady

425
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:23,920
took off her clothes,

426
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:24,880
why didn't you remind her?

427
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:25,440
Remind her?

428
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,030
If I had reminded her,

429
00:18:26,030 --> 00:18:26,590
wouldn't she have known

430
00:18:26,590 --> 00:18:27,880
that I'm not blind?

431
00:18:28,830 --> 00:18:29,960
You let it slip, didn't you?

432
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,310
Isn't this still a scam?

433
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:33,400
Alright.

434
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:35,110
That hurts.

435
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:36,580
You deserve it.

436
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,240
You deserve to be beaten.

437
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,200
I must report you.

438
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,640
No, no, no. Liu.

439
00:18:41,030 --> 00:18:41,720
Seriously,

440
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:42,960
stay and be a masseur here.

441
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:44,240
I'm really short-staffed here.

442
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,110
I won't do it.

443
00:18:46,270 --> 00:18:47,070
Free training,

444
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:47,750
a base salary of 3,000,

445
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:48,720
and commissions.

446
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,000
I won't do it
no matter how much you pay me.

447
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,830
Why are you so stubborn?

448
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:54,680
Another scammer?

449
00:18:55,830 --> 00:18:56,640
Who is it?

450
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:00,830
Looks pretty real.

451
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:03,920
You sneaked up on me again?

452
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,580
You sneaked up on my daughter.

453
00:19:06,550 --> 00:19:07,350
Your daughter?

454
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:09,270
My biological daughter. Got a problem?

455
00:19:09,270 --> 00:19:10,240
Dad, who is it?

456
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:11,440
A new staff member?

457
00:19:12,270 --> 00:19:13,350
I took in an apprentice.

458
00:19:13,350 --> 00:19:15,080
I'm teaching him acupressure.

459
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,750
Morning.

460
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:21,400
Morning.

461
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:25,110
What are you looking at?

462
00:19:25,110 --> 00:19:26,310
Look at this guy.

463
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,000
Jumping rope.

464
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,510
What is he doing?

465
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,400
He's a young man after all.

466
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,270
So full of energy.

467
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:50,120
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

468
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,160
Why are you copying Zhengliang?

469
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,200
He taught me this.

470
00:19:58,830 --> 00:20:01,030
He was going through
something big back then.

471
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:02,360
What's your reason now?

472
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:04,410
I'm going through something too.

473
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,510
About the surgery?

474
00:20:14,590 --> 00:20:15,590
The surgery

475
00:20:17,510 --> 00:20:18,920
really makes me anxious.

476
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:27,920
If you're so afraid of surgery,

477
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:31,620
why did you choose to specialize
in surgery in the first place?

478
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,550
My dad chose it for me.

479
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,900
Let's not talk about this.

480
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:42,160
I've been overthinking lately.

481
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:44,160
Once I start,

482
00:20:45,270 --> 00:20:46,310
I can't sleep.

483
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,270
When I can't sleep,

484
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,830
I feel terrible.

485
00:20:52,310 --> 00:20:53,770
Then I keep thinking about

486
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,100
making mistakes during surgery.

487
00:20:58,070 --> 00:20:58,880
Can't sleep

488
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,490
and then feel terrible—

489
00:21:02,070 --> 00:21:03,270
it's a vicious cycle.

490
00:21:04,790 --> 00:21:05,830
That won't do.

491
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:09,240
How about this?

492
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:11,440
I'll prescribe you some sleeping pills.

493
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,840
Taking those won't work.

494
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:16,490
It only treats the symptoms,
not the root cause.

495
00:21:18,550 --> 00:21:20,550
Do you have any other ideas?

496
00:21:24,310 --> 00:21:25,350
I do.

497
00:21:26,310 --> 00:21:28,310
I went through the same phase as you.

498
00:21:28,310 --> 00:21:29,270
When I was a kid,

499
00:21:29,590 --> 00:21:31,120
I got nervous before exams.

500
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,440
But my way of dealing with it

501
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:35,940
won't work for you.

502
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,880
You haven't even told me.

503
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,000
How do you know it won't work?

504
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:42,680
When...

505
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:44,830
When I get nervous,

506
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,680
I sing the sing-and-dance duet.

507
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:52,070
♪ Rushing out ♪

508
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:54,510
♪ Rushing out ♪

509
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,240
♪ Clomp, clomp, down the stairs ♪

510
00:21:56,270 --> 00:21:58,160
♪ Clomp, clomp, down the stairs ♪

511
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,920
♪ Walk a mile or two down the road ♪

512
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,920
♪ Walk a mile or two down the road ♪

513
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,550
♪ Past four or five villages ♪

514
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:05,510
♪ Past four or five villages ♪

515
00:22:05,550 --> 00:22:07,350
♪ Over six or seven pavilions ♪

516
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,310
♪ Over six or seven pavilions ♪

517
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:12,590
♪ With eight, nine, or ten flowers,
to the west wing I go ♪

518
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:16,750
♪ With eight, nine, or ten flowers,
to the west wing I go ♪

519
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:19,400
♪ How far is the west wing? ♪

520
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:22,270
♪ How far is the west wing? ♪

521
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:26,350
♪ It's just on the other side
of the wall ♪

522
00:22:27,510 --> 00:22:31,830
♪ It's just on the other side
of the wall ♪

523
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,590
Alright.

524
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,000
Am I...

525
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,070
Not bad. Not bad.

526
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,400
Well...

527
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:43,590
Mingming, can you...

528
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:45,930
sing the whole thing for me?

529
00:22:46,790 --> 00:22:47,590
Sure.

530
00:22:47,790 --> 00:22:48,590
Okay.

531
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:50,680
Here, hold this.

532
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:57,070
♪ Rushing out ♪

533
00:22:57,270 --> 00:22:58,680
♪ Clomp, clomp, down the stairs ♪

534
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,550
♪ Walk a mile or two down the road ♪

535
00:23:00,590 --> 00:23:02,160
♪ Past four or five villages ♪

536
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:03,920
♪ Over six or seven pavilions ♪

537
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:07,270
♪ With eight, nine, or ten flowers,
to the west wing I go ♪

538
00:23:23,590 --> 00:23:24,400
Thank you.

539
00:23:25,550 --> 00:23:27,110
You need to get this straight.

540
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:28,790
ID card,

541
00:23:28,790 --> 00:23:30,030
phone number, and the date.

542
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:31,720
They all need to be written clearly.

543
00:23:31,720 --> 00:23:33,270
Hello, remember me?

544
00:23:33,310 --> 00:23:34,200
Mr. Liu.

545
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:34,750
Yes.

546
00:23:34,750 --> 00:23:36,680
Have you found my luggage?

547
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:38,200
Well...

548
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,570
we haven't found it yet.

549
00:23:39,830 --> 00:23:40,070
Come on.

550
00:23:40,070 --> 00:23:42,000
Is it that hard
to find a piece of luggage?

551
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,030
Wasn't it taken by the old lady

552
00:23:43,030 --> 00:23:44,200
in the bunk beneath me?

553
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:44,720
Right?

554
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,480
Can't you find her ticket info

555
00:23:46,510 --> 00:23:47,110
and phone number,

556
00:23:47,110 --> 00:23:48,400
and then call her?

557
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:49,880
Yes, about this matter,

558
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:50,880
we have been

559
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:52,240
actively dealing with it.

560
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,240
But we really haven't found

561
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,110
that old lady yet.

562
00:23:54,110 --> 00:23:54,920
If there are any new developments,

563
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:55,750
I will definitely

564
00:23:55,750 --> 00:23:57,000
notify you immediately, okay?

565
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,110
I'm really sorry.

566
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,270
What's the use of apologizing?

567
00:23:59,270 --> 00:24:00,530
Don't apologize to me.

568
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:03,880
I'm also waiting for updates anyway.

569
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,200
This is the situation now.

570
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,600
There's nothing I can do.

571
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,330
Where are we going next?

572
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,270
What do you mean "we?"

573
00:24:18,030 --> 00:24:19,760
What does it have to do with you?

574
00:24:20,510 --> 00:24:21,350
You've been following me all day.

575
00:24:21,350 --> 00:24:22,750
What exactly do you want?

576
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:25,000
You want to make money off me, right?

577
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,160
Let me tell you,
I have no money. I'm very poor.

578
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:29,200
Yes, I can see you're poor.

579
00:24:29,590 --> 00:24:31,190
I'm not doing this for money.

580
00:24:31,510 --> 00:24:33,110
I just think you're interesting.

581
00:24:33,110 --> 00:24:34,070
I can definitely

582
00:24:34,070 --> 00:24:35,670
have some fun following you.

583
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:37,680
Isn't this more interesting than

584
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,590
playing games in that internet cafe?

585
00:24:39,590 --> 00:24:41,120
You're quite interesting.

586
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,310
You're like

587
00:24:42,310 --> 00:24:43,110
a stubborn, obnoxious

588
00:24:43,110 --> 00:24:44,310
piece of crap.

589
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:45,310
I swear

590
00:24:45,310 --> 00:24:47,480
I'll go back to the hotel
and check out right now.

591
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,160
Get out of my sight immediately,

592
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:50,440
or I'll call the police.

593
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:51,750
What will you tell the police?

594
00:24:51,750 --> 00:24:52,550
That you're stalking me.

595
00:24:52,550 --> 00:24:53,680
But we're friends.

596
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:54,720
Who said we're friends?

597
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:55,480
I don't even know

598
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,310
your name.

599
00:24:58,510 --> 00:24:59,750
My name is Zhou Zheng.

600
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,690
"Zhou Zheng" as in "handsome."

601
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:03,320
You can also call me Pink.

602
00:25:05,030 --> 00:25:06,960
Come on, Uncle, let's shake hands.

603
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:09,900
Call me Uncle again, and I'll beat you up.

604
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,310
Bro.

605
00:25:13,270 --> 00:25:15,000
I'll call you bro. Is that okay?

606
00:25:26,350 --> 00:25:27,880
Do you have nothing to do?

607
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,310
I really don't.

608
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:31,000
If you have nothing to do,
why don't you go to school?

609
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,110
I already did.

610
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:34,540
Let me tell you,

611
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:36,200
when I was in school,

612
00:25:36,270 --> 00:25:38,330
my grades were actually pretty good.

613
00:25:39,750 --> 00:25:40,790
But I think

614
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,410
going to school is useless.

615
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:46,000
Your grades were good?

616
00:25:47,200 --> 00:25:47,920
I've never seen

617
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,000
anyone with good grades

618
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,310
sporting pink hair.

619
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:54,200
I'm just letting myself go.

620
00:25:55,270 --> 00:25:56,350
If you don't want to go to school,

621
00:25:56,350 --> 00:25:57,510
go find a job.

622
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:01,590
Bro.

623
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:04,310
Even a medical doctor like you

624
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:05,550
can't find a job.

625
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:08,240
How could a high school dropout like me

626
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:09,350
find one so easily?

627
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,680
Who said I can't find a job?

628
00:26:12,110 --> 00:26:12,960
I'm in high demand.

629
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,890
How many times do I have to tell you?

630
00:26:16,790 --> 00:26:18,830
I can see that. Very much in demand.

631
00:26:19,830 --> 00:26:20,510
Bro.

632
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:22,590
Finding a job

633
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:24,400
takes time.

634
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:26,920
You sent your resume to so many hospitals.

635
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,720
They need a few days to review it.

636
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:32,820
How about this?

637
00:26:33,310 --> 00:26:36,030
It's rare for you to come to Bengbu.

638
00:26:37,400 --> 00:26:38,790
I'll show you around.

639
00:26:39,350 --> 00:26:40,280
Not interested.

640
00:26:42,960 --> 00:26:43,750
My treat.

641
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:47,750
Taxi, meals—

642
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:49,880
all expenses are on me.

643
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:51,510
Generous enough?

644
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,980
What's wrong with you?

645
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,160
Are you after my kidneys?

646
00:26:58,350 --> 00:26:58,960
Bro,

647
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:01,120
what are you talking about?

648
00:27:01,880 --> 00:27:03,680
Do I look that much like a bad guy?

649
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:06,350
I'm just bored.

650
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:12,680
Give me another discount on my room.

651
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:14,790
50 is already a huge discount.

652
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:19,310
40.

653
00:27:19,310 --> 00:27:19,960
20.

654
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:20,400
38.

655
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:21,110
25.

656
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:21,880
30!

657
00:27:23,070 --> 00:27:24,030
30 a day.

658
00:27:24,350 --> 00:27:25,590
Not a penny less.

659
00:27:25,590 --> 00:27:27,920
Any less and I'll lose my shirt.

660
00:27:31,830 --> 00:27:32,640
Is there anything good to eat

661
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:33,920
around here?

662
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,400
You asked the right person.

663
00:27:39,380 --> 00:27:40,080
♪ What're you looking at? ♪

664
00:27:41,330 --> 00:27:42,160
♪ I'm not looking at you ♪

665
00:27:44,130 --> 00:27:44,700
♪ Alright then ♪

666
00:27:45,750 --> 00:27:46,110
♪ Come on ♪

667
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:50,930
♪ The sun's already high
and I'm just getting downstairs ♪

668
00:27:50,490 --> 00:27:53,950
[Future] [Happiness]

669
00:27:51,210 --> 00:27:53,210
♪ My hair is a flattened mess,
like a bird's nest ♪

670
00:27:53,890 --> 00:27:55,840
♪ There is nothing much in my pockets ♪

671
00:27:56,100 --> 00:27:58,200
♪ I still sway a little as I walk ♪

672
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:00,240
♪ A buddy at the door calls out to me ♪

673
00:28:00,310 --> 00:28:01,500
♪ Where are you off to? ♪

674
00:28:01,570 --> 00:28:02,760
♪ I say I don't know yet ♪

675
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,140
♪ Just gonna head on forward ♪

676
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:06,830
♪ And see where I end up ♪

677
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:09,340
♪ Anyway, there isn't much to do
at home ♪

678
00:28:10,090 --> 00:28:10,780
♪ Just wandering around ♪

679
00:28:11,270 --> 00:28:12,100
♪ Just wandering around ♪

680
00:28:12,340 --> 00:28:14,060
♪ Always wandering around ♪

681
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:16,280
♪ Look to the left ♪

682
00:28:16,590 --> 00:28:17,420
♪ Look to the right ♪

683
00:28:17,710 --> 00:28:19,650
♪ Whose doorway
has a crowd gathered around it? ♪

684
00:28:19,870 --> 00:28:20,670
♪ What're you looking at? ♪

685
00:28:21,470 --> 00:28:22,340
♪ I'm joining the fun ♪

686
00:28:22,740 --> 00:28:25,080
♪ There's no fun to join ♪

687
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:25,960
You're having the worst luck.

688
00:28:25,510 --> 00:28:26,350
♪ There's nothing to see here ♪

689
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:27,770
♪ Bored out of my mind ♪

690
00:28:28,030 --> 00:28:30,540
♪ I just can't keep up with you ♪

691
00:28:30,110 --> 00:28:31,370
It's not a big problem.

692
00:28:31,580 --> 00:28:32,740
♪ Oh my ♪

693
00:28:33,140 --> 00:28:34,080
♪ I may be broke ♪

694
00:28:33,510 --> 00:28:35,510
Eat up. Eat more. Finish it.

695
00:28:34,290 --> 00:28:35,990
♪ But we still have to look the part ♪

696
00:28:35,830 --> 00:28:37,070
If it's not enough, you can have my bowl.

697
00:28:36,970 --> 00:28:37,770
♪ Just wandering around ♪

698
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:38,880
Mr. Bird,
what have you been eating lately?

699
00:28:38,290 --> 00:28:39,080
♪ Just wandering around ♪

700
00:28:39,540 --> 00:28:42,080
♪ Young people
don't make that many plans ♪

701
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:41,690
You've got the runs pretty bad.

702
00:28:42,330 --> 00:28:44,420
♪ The sun's pretty nice today ♪

703
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:43,850
Do you have tissues?

704
00:28:44,850 --> 00:28:47,400
♪ Let's go out and not waste the day ♪

705
00:28:46,920 --> 00:28:47,790
This is

706
00:28:47,790 --> 00:28:50,310
the most famous sculpture in Zhucheng.

707
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:52,720
I think some master sculptor made it.

708
00:28:51,790 --> 00:28:55,190
[Marker of the North-South Divide
in China]

709
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:56,690
Look at that.

710
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:00,310
Blue is north.

711
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:01,480
Red is south.

712
00:29:02,830 --> 00:29:03,760
What do you mean?

713
00:29:04,510 --> 00:29:05,310
Bengbu

714
00:29:05,590 --> 00:29:08,990
is on the dividing line
between northern and southern China.

715
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:10,750
Look.

716
00:29:10,860 --> 00:29:14,870
[For Dramatic Purposes Only.
Do Not Imitate.]

717
00:29:13,550 --> 00:29:14,950
This is the north, right?

718
00:29:17,070 --> 00:29:18,200
I'm in the south now.

719
00:29:20,030 --> 00:29:21,430
Now I'm back in the north.

720
00:29:22,830 --> 00:29:24,560
Look, I'm back in the south now.

721
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:29,480
I call this traveling extensively.

722
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,350
Wow, amazing.

723
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:32,590
You try it.

724
00:29:31,570 --> 00:29:38,800
[Marker of the North-South Divide
in China]

725
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,830
I won't.

726
00:29:33,830 --> 00:29:35,350
Since we're here. Come on.

727
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:35,960
Come on.

728
00:29:38,750 --> 00:29:40,280
Every time I jump like this,

729
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,200
it brings me good luck.

730
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,030
I think

731
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:44,560
you're a bit unlucky today.

732
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,830
Try jumping a few times.

733
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,720
Maybe your bad luck will go away.

734
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:51,400
Try it.

735
00:29:54,540 --> 00:29:57,990
[For Dramatic Purposes Only.
Do Not Imitate.]

736
00:30:00,480 --> 00:30:01,310
In the north.

737
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,000
Back in the south.

738
00:30:04,110 --> 00:30:05,310
In the north again.

739
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:10,240
Boring.

740
00:30:13,070 --> 00:30:14,400
Jump back to the south!

741
00:30:16,030 --> 00:30:16,830
Zhengliang.

742
00:30:17,110 --> 00:30:18,920
Let's go to the amusement park tomorrow.

743
00:30:18,920 --> 00:30:20,480
I want to ride the roller coaster.

744
00:30:20,480 --> 00:30:21,280
I'm not going.

745
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:24,500
I'm going to stay in my room
and look at job postings.

746
00:30:24,510 --> 00:30:28,120
[Zheng's Dental Clinic]

747
00:30:24,720 --> 00:30:26,070
I'll help you look later.

748
00:30:26,070 --> 00:30:26,960
I promise I'll find

749
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:28,200
10 more hospitals for you tonight.

750
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:29,200
I'm still not going.

751
00:30:28,230 --> 00:30:31,230
[Jiajiale Department Store]

752
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:31,070
Running around outside with you

753
00:30:31,070 --> 00:30:33,000
is more tiring than doing surgery.

754
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:34,830
Well,

755
00:30:34,890 --> 00:30:39,830
[Zheng's Dental Clinic]

756
00:30:35,200 --> 00:30:36,070
why don't you tell me

757
00:30:36,070 --> 00:30:38,070
about the most difficult

758
00:30:38,070 --> 00:30:39,530
surgery you've ever done?

759
00:30:39,590 --> 00:30:41,450
You wouldn't understand anyway.

760
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,480
Just tell me.

761
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:47,400
Have you ever

762
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:49,240
brought someone back to life

763
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,200
when they were

764
00:30:51,200 --> 00:30:52,310
definitely going to die?

765
00:30:52,310 --> 00:30:54,310
That's contradictory.

766
00:30:54,590 --> 00:30:57,790
If they can be saved,
they're not definitely going to die.

767
00:30:58,960 --> 00:30:59,640
Come on.

768
00:30:59,640 --> 00:31:01,070
You definitely know

769
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:02,640
what I mean.

770
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:04,310
True.

771
00:31:04,790 --> 00:31:05,480
If you really had

772
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,680
such great skills,

773
00:31:07,350 --> 00:31:09,240
you wouldn't have trouble finding a job.

774
00:31:09,240 --> 00:31:11,000
I've told you 100 times.

775
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,680
I encountered an unexpected situation

776
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:14,030
and am going through a rough patch.

777
00:31:14,030 --> 00:31:14,920
Understand?

778
00:31:19,070 --> 00:31:19,880
I understand.

779
00:31:20,510 --> 00:31:21,910
It's like playing a game.

780
00:31:22,440 --> 00:31:23,510
There's a network lag,

781
00:31:23,510 --> 00:31:24,840
and the screen freezes.

782
00:31:31,510 --> 00:31:33,040
Someone is looking for you.

783
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:34,720
Who?

784
00:31:36,550 --> 00:31:37,110
Me.

785
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:43,080
Do we still have anything to talk about?

786
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,000
Big Brother.

787
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:53,000
How did you find me here?

788
00:31:54,310 --> 00:31:55,110
What?

789
00:31:57,270 --> 00:31:58,310
Did you fall in love with me?

790
00:31:58,310 --> 00:31:59,200
Oh my goodness.

791
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:01,000
You still dare to be so glib here?

792
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:03,250
Aren't you afraid of death?

793
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:10,090
This place is small.

794
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,300
There's no room for fighting.

795
00:32:13,030 --> 00:32:14,490
Let's go outside and talk.

796
00:32:21,070 --> 00:32:22,130
Don't play tricks.

797
00:32:42,270 --> 00:32:43,400
Call the police now.

798
00:32:43,720 --> 00:32:44,750
Why?

799
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:45,750
Those people are here

800
00:32:45,750 --> 00:32:47,350
to make trouble for your son.

801
00:32:47,350 --> 00:32:48,110
Let them.

802
00:32:48,110 --> 00:32:49,640
It has nothing to do with me.

803
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:52,510
He's young and ignorant.

804
00:32:52,510 --> 00:32:53,070
But as his mother,

805
00:32:53,070 --> 00:32:54,200
how can you say that?

806
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:56,270
So what should I say?

807
00:32:56,920 --> 00:32:57,920
I just said a few words to him,

808
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,270
and he cut ties with me.

809
00:32:59,270 --> 00:33:00,640
Fine by me.

810
00:33:08,590 --> 00:33:09,590
They're really hitting him.

811
00:33:09,590 --> 00:33:10,520
Call the police.

812
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:11,970
He's your son after all.

813
00:33:12,640 --> 00:33:14,030
If I can't keep him in line,

814
00:33:14,030 --> 00:33:15,510
let society do it.

815
00:33:15,590 --> 00:33:17,320
That's fine. I won't stop them.

816
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:19,380
If you want to call the police,

817
00:33:19,510 --> 00:33:20,920
go outside and do it.

818
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,310
If the police come,

819
00:33:22,310 --> 00:33:24,240
I won't be able to do business here.

820
00:33:24,310 --> 00:33:25,160
Landlady!

821
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:27,510
There's no hot water on the second floor!

822
00:33:27,510 --> 00:33:28,400
Coming!

823
00:33:29,110 --> 00:33:30,310
The work never ends.

824
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:31,480
Coming!

825
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:34,080
Are you really not going to do anything?

826
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,860
What kind of person is she?

827
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:45,900
Do it again.

828
00:33:51,510 --> 00:33:52,480
No wonder

829
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:55,400
your girlfriend says you're a weak man.

830
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:56,680
You hit like a wimp.

831
00:33:57,830 --> 00:33:59,030
Here. Slap this side.

832
00:34:04,200 --> 00:34:05,000
Keep going.

833
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,720
Big Brother,

834
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:09,440
that slap was great.

835
00:34:09,510 --> 00:34:10,800
How could it be so amazing?

836
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:11,590
Keep going. Don't stop.

837
00:34:11,590 --> 00:34:12,280
Come on.

838
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,380
Put the phone down!

839
00:34:14,230 --> 00:34:15,590
Stop yelling here.

840
00:34:16,630 --> 00:34:17,690
This is my brother.

841
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:19,429
He has a heart condition.

842
00:34:19,630 --> 00:34:21,510
If you want to hit him, beat him to death.

843
00:34:21,510 --> 00:34:22,230
That way, our family

844
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:23,710
can get compensation.

845
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:25,760
Then I'll have money to get a wife

846
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:26,800
and buy a house.

847
00:34:27,510 --> 00:34:28,800
Who are you trying to scare?

848
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:30,230
I'm not scaring you.

849
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:31,150
I'm cheering for you.

850
00:34:31,150 --> 00:34:32,110
Come on. Keep going.

851
00:34:32,110 --> 00:34:33,360
-Come on.
-Take his phone!

852
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:35,159
Lay a finger on me and you'll see.

853
00:34:35,510 --> 00:34:36,440
Just a reminder.

854
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:38,070
I called the police.

855
00:34:38,070 --> 00:34:39,000
If you want to hit him, hurry up.

856
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,600
-Come on. Hurry up.
-Come on.

857
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:42,730
Beat me to death!

858
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:47,550
If you dare talk nonsense to the police,

859
00:34:47,550 --> 00:34:48,800
I'll burn your shop down!

860
00:34:48,800 --> 00:34:49,860
I'll remember you!

861
00:34:51,110 --> 00:34:51,800
Come on!

862
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:07,490
Whoever backs down is a coward!

863
00:35:12,510 --> 00:35:14,400
Alright, they're gone.

864
00:35:20,150 --> 00:35:20,960
Are you okay?

865
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:24,850
It's no big deal.

866
00:35:25,920 --> 00:35:27,550
I'll be fine after some sleep.

867
00:35:27,550 --> 00:35:29,410
How did you provoke that bald guy?

868
00:35:33,150 --> 00:35:34,750
I slept with his girlfriend.

869
00:35:36,670 --> 00:35:38,000
You really deserved it.

870
00:35:40,280 --> 00:35:41,190
Can you walk?

871
00:35:41,230 --> 00:35:42,760
I'll take you to the hospital.

872
00:35:42,760 --> 00:35:44,020
Who are you insulting?

873
00:35:52,670 --> 00:35:53,760
Wow, amazing.

874
00:35:56,550 --> 00:35:59,440
It won't stop me
from riding the roller coaster tomorrow.

875
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,230
Don't you understand my words?

876
00:36:00,230 --> 00:36:01,360
I said I'm not going.

877
00:36:01,710 --> 00:36:02,510
Come on.

878
00:36:04,190 --> 00:36:05,510
I even got beaten up.

879
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:07,720
Can't you just

880
00:36:08,190 --> 00:36:09,190
grant me this one

881
00:36:09,190 --> 00:36:10,230
small wish?

882
00:36:10,230 --> 00:36:11,110
Do you think I'm Aladdin's lamp?

883
00:36:11,110 --> 00:36:12,360
Granting your wish?

884
00:36:12,550 --> 00:36:13,440
Go by yourself.

885
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,630
Don't get handsy with me!

886
00:36:15,630 --> 00:36:16,190
Bro!

887
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:19,230
Brother!

888
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:23,070
I'm scared to do it alone.

889
00:36:23,070 --> 00:36:23,880
Don't push your luck.

890
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:24,710
You disgust me.

891
00:36:24,710 --> 00:36:25,910
I'm not your brother!

892
00:36:27,920 --> 00:36:29,800
You just admitted right here

893
00:36:29,800 --> 00:36:31,060
that I'm your brother.

894
00:36:31,710 --> 00:36:33,840
How could you change your tune so fast?

895
00:36:35,070 --> 00:36:37,070
Yes, I do have a younger brother.

896
00:36:37,710 --> 00:36:39,440
He's an idiot just like you,

897
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:40,800
but he's not you.

898
00:36:42,440 --> 00:36:43,500
You have a brother?

899
00:36:44,630 --> 00:36:46,160
Do you have the same mother?

900
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,960
What does it have to do with you?
Get lost.

901
00:36:47,960 --> 00:36:49,280
I just want to know.

902
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:52,630
Let me guess his name.

903
00:36:54,710 --> 00:36:55,630
Liu Zheng'an?

904
00:36:57,710 --> 00:36:58,400
No?

905
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:00,780
Liu Zhengdeng?

906
00:37:05,800 --> 00:37:06,760
Liu Zhengjian!

907
00:37:07,510 --> 00:37:09,070
You're "jian" (low).

908
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:18,490
[Dream Garden Themed Hotel]

909
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:13,670
I was just kidding.

910
00:37:15,630 --> 00:37:16,440
Zhengliang!

911
00:37:48,670 --> 00:37:50,550
Still working this late?

912
00:37:50,760 --> 00:37:51,400
Look.

913
00:37:52,070 --> 00:37:52,760
You must be hungry.

914
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:53,880
I made you some late night snacks.

915
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:55,080
Eat it while it's hot.

916
00:37:55,360 --> 00:37:56,160
Wait a minute.

917
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:56,880
How could you

918
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:58,070
just walk into my room?

919
00:37:58,070 --> 00:37:59,930
This is an invasion of my privacy.

920
00:38:03,070 --> 00:38:04,110
We're not strangers.

921
00:38:04,110 --> 00:38:05,510
Aren't we family now?

922
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,490
You're friends with my son,

923
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:09,590
so you're like half a son to me.

924
00:38:12,550 --> 00:38:14,010
I'm not your son's friend.

925
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:17,110
Besides, I'm only a few years
younger than you.

926
00:38:17,110 --> 00:38:18,320
I can't be your son.

927
00:38:19,510 --> 00:38:20,550
I don't eat late night snacks.

928
00:38:20,550 --> 00:38:21,320
Take it away,

929
00:38:21,320 --> 00:38:22,980
and close the door behind you.

930
00:38:26,230 --> 00:38:27,070
Young man.

931
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,150
Sometimes,

932
00:38:29,630 --> 00:38:30,360
food

933
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:31,510
is not just for filling

934
00:38:31,510 --> 00:38:32,750
your stomach.

935
00:38:33,190 --> 00:38:35,000
It's for filling your heart.

936
00:38:37,230 --> 00:38:39,230
You're all alone in a strange place,

937
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:40,760
working in the middle of the night.

938
00:38:40,760 --> 00:38:42,110
How can you go hungry?

939
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:44,110
If your mother knew,

940
00:38:44,110 --> 00:38:45,360
how sad she would be.

941
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:49,880
Come on. Eat up.

942
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,520
I know you're hungry.

943
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:52,800
Come on.

944
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,760
These are my specialties.

945
00:38:56,510 --> 00:38:57,320
Try them.

946
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:59,110
They taste like home.

947
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:00,360
Taste like home?

948
00:39:01,480 --> 00:39:02,320
How much is it?

949
00:39:04,190 --> 00:39:04,960
The rice,

950
00:39:05,550 --> 00:39:06,550
these two dishes,

951
00:39:07,670 --> 00:39:09,150
the chopsticks, the bowl,

952
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:12,090
and this tray—you charge for them, right?

953
00:39:12,630 --> 00:39:14,230
How much? Give me a number.

954
00:39:26,230 --> 00:39:27,670
I raised my son to be useless,

955
00:39:27,670 --> 00:39:28,630
and that's fine,

956
00:39:29,670 --> 00:39:31,190
but someone like you...

957
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,010
I just want to ask you one thing.

958
00:39:37,920 --> 00:39:39,840
Does an educated person like you

959
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:41,400
also not believe

960
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:43,730
that there is true kindness in this world?

961
00:39:52,010 --> 00:39:55,730
[Accommodation]

962
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:00,440
How does it taste?

963
00:40:12,340 --> 00:40:14,470
[WeChat Pay Recommended]

964
00:40:12,670 --> 00:40:14,070
80, fixed price.

965
00:40:14,630 --> 00:40:16,160
Just scan the QR code to pay.

966
00:40:23,070 --> 00:40:24,530
You really are his mother.

967
00:40:27,960 --> 00:40:29,930
[Health Conservation]

968
00:40:30,630 --> 00:40:31,510
You were the one nagging about wanting

969
00:40:31,510 --> 00:40:32,770
radish meatball soup.

970
00:40:33,070 --> 00:40:34,190
My wife got up early

971
00:40:34,190 --> 00:40:35,440
just to make it for you.

972
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:36,800
And you just took such a tiny sip?

973
00:40:36,800 --> 00:40:38,440
Aren't you just messing with us?

974
00:40:38,440 --> 00:40:39,840
Who can drink

975
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:40,920
this greasy

976
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:42,650
meat soup early in the morning?

977
00:40:43,550 --> 00:40:44,400
Alright, alright.

978
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,920
Don't make her
go to all that trouble anymore.

979
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:47,180
Do you think we want to?

980
00:40:47,400 --> 00:40:48,320
We're already exhausted

981
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:49,150
from work every day!

982
00:40:49,150 --> 00:40:50,400
And we have to be here
to take care of you!

983
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:51,230
Then just do

984
00:40:51,230 --> 00:40:52,150
your own thing.

985
00:40:52,150 --> 00:40:52,960
I...

986
00:40:52,960 --> 00:40:54,280
I don't need you to take care of me.

987
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:55,230
What did you tell the nurse?

988
00:40:55,230 --> 00:40:56,230
What did I say?

989
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:57,480
That we don't care about you!

990
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,550
Did you say that?

991
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:00,550
Now you're pretending to be polite to me.

992
00:41:00,550 --> 00:41:01,670
Stop pretending!

993
00:41:01,960 --> 00:41:03,090
When people get old,

994
00:41:03,880 --> 00:41:05,410
they just become annoying.

995
00:41:07,710 --> 00:41:09,110
If your mom were alive,

996
00:41:09,110 --> 00:41:10,230
-You're doing this again.
-I wouldn't have...

997
00:41:10,230 --> 00:41:11,030
You're pulling this stunt again,

998
00:41:11,030 --> 00:41:11,760
aren't you?

999
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:13,400
We told you to have surgery,
and you refused.

1000
00:41:13,400 --> 00:41:14,360
You're just lying here every day.

1001
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:15,280
Who are you trying

1002
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:16,400
to get sympathy from?

1003
00:41:16,400 --> 00:41:17,670
Do you own a mountain of gold or silver?

1004
00:41:17,670 --> 00:41:18,710
Doesn't surgery cost money?

1005
00:41:18,710 --> 00:41:20,110
Do whatever you want!

1006
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,200
Nobody cares!

1007
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:33,440
Bed 35, how are you feeling today?

1008
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,190
Not bad.

1009
00:41:35,670 --> 00:41:36,670
Where is Li?

1010
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:37,840
He went out.

1011
00:41:38,150 --> 00:41:39,190
He went out?

1012
00:41:45,830 --> 00:41:48,410
[Nurses' Station]

1013
00:41:54,070 --> 00:41:55,190
Where is Bed 36?

1014
00:41:55,440 --> 00:41:57,030
He went to the bathroom, I think.

1015
00:41:57,030 --> 00:41:57,840
You think?

1016
00:41:57,920 --> 00:41:59,380
How long has he been there?

1017
00:42:00,630 --> 00:42:01,760
20 minutes.

1018
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:03,000
What if he fell

1019
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:03,930
in the bathroom?

1020
00:42:04,030 --> 00:42:06,030
Hurry up and get a man to check on him.

1021
00:42:07,670 --> 00:42:08,930
Chief Physician Tong.

1022
00:42:16,670 --> 00:42:17,360
Is he there?

1023
00:42:17,360 --> 00:42:18,290
He's not inside.

1024
00:42:18,970 --> 00:42:20,400
I just checked.

1025
00:42:20,510 --> 00:42:21,360
Li's shoes and coat

1026
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,360
are gone.

1027
00:42:22,630 --> 00:42:24,030
He has Alzheimer's.

1028
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:25,630
If he really wanders off in the hospital,

1029
00:42:25,630 --> 00:42:27,110
even if he left on his own,

1030
00:42:27,110 --> 00:42:29,000
we will have to bear
most of the responsibility.

1031
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:29,800
Have someone stay behind.

1032
00:42:29,800 --> 00:42:31,280
Tell everyone else who's available

1033
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:32,540
to search every floor.

1034
00:42:32,630 --> 00:42:33,670
I'll go to the first floor
to check the surveillance.

1035
00:42:33,670 --> 00:42:34,320
Okay.

1036
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:37,660
Going home after work?

1037
00:42:37,880 --> 00:42:39,190
Why haven't you left yet?

1038
00:42:39,190 --> 00:42:40,390
I was waiting for you.

1039
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:41,230
Why were you waiting for me?

1040
00:42:41,230 --> 00:42:42,290
Can I walk you home?

1041
00:42:43,190 --> 00:42:44,590
Why? Is something wrong?

1042
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:46,480
I just feel so uptight.

1043
00:42:46,480 --> 00:42:47,540
I can't relax.

1044
00:42:48,030 --> 00:42:50,150
Can you teach me
a couple of sing-and-dance duets?

1045
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:51,880
Didn't you say it doesn't work?

1046
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:55,360
As long as it distracts me,

1047
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:56,760
I'll do whatever you say.

1048
00:42:58,710 --> 00:43:00,360
Then you might as well go to a bar,

1049
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:01,920
find a beautiful woman
to have a drink with,

1050
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:03,030
and then treat her to a meal.

1051
00:43:03,030 --> 00:43:04,630
If you succeed,
you're the one who benefits.

1052
00:43:04,630 --> 00:43:05,630
If you fail,

1053
00:43:05,630 --> 00:43:07,400
at least it'll help you
blow off some steam.

1054
00:43:07,400 --> 00:43:08,000
Wait a minute.

1055
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,260
You two, wait a minute!

1056
00:43:10,230 --> 00:43:11,320
Li is missing.
